      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 5633
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-25T21:02:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is the purpose of this template just for type safety between PaintersDepth and DisjointStencilIndex? I\u0027m wondering where this can be an issue, and if we could also use something like more specific function names in cases where these might be accidentally mixed up.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "2e4f657d145b29c68531e8479f94a8948227e610",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c561612d_82bc8378",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/DrawOrder.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-26T00:29:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For type safety between PaintersDepth, DisjointStencilIndex, and CompressedPaintersOrder.\n\nI think function names could help, but I really wanted security in preventing them from being mismatched. If they are all uint16_t\u0027s and you pass in 3 of them and accidentally swizzle them around, it might not be obvious to spot and could lead to hard to replicate bugs because the draw will be sorted incorrectly.\n\nThis all should compile down to just 16-bits of storage and the \u0027using\u0027s make it so that actual use cases don\u0027t really care about the Sequence template parameter.",
      "parentUuid": "0634c522_a39d541d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "2e4f657d145b29c68531e8479f94a8948227e610",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
